hexagon: replay the packed batches of a graph of more than one batch

Base: llama.cpp commit c6824a9 plus every patch of the series before this one.

The defect

The batch cache replays only a graph that fits in one DSP batch. A decode token
of the 4B Q8_0 needs 4 batches, thus the host packs each token again. In a chat
on the phone, the stage of the fixed costs measured a pack of 2.1 ms for each
decode token, and the host times (LLAMA_HOSTPROF) show "replays 0".

The change

While the host packs a graph whose first batch is empty, flush_batch keeps a
copy of each batch that it sends. Such a copy is a head of the snapshot, with
its buffers in the sorted sequence of flush_batch. batch_snapshot keeps the
heads and the last batch, when no batch holds the unfused ops of a state chain.
batch_replay checks each batch as before: the data pointer and the buffer of
each tensor, the op params, and the slot index of each fused state op. Then it
sends each head, and it loads the last batch into the op batch, as for a graph
of one batch.

With GGML_HEXAGON_BATCHCACHE=2 the fresh packing runs before the replay sends a
batch. flush_batch keeps the batches of the fresh packing (capture_hold) and
does not send them. When a batch differs, the fresh packing goes out in place
of the replay. The switch GGML_HEXAGON_BATCHCACHE_MULTI (preset 1) gives 0:
only a graph of one batch has a replay.

The tests

The test mode of tests/fuzz/hexhost gives 0 findings in the configurations
none, asan, ubsan, tsan and msan, each with the debug and the release profile.
Its symbolic check compares the result of each step on the device with the
meaning of the graph. The harness sets batch sizes of 1 to 1280 ops and a VA
limit of 64 MiB, thus many graphs need more than one batch. On the regression
inputs and a corpus of 503 inputs of 2 minutes of fuzzing, 287 replays had 1 to
30 heads, and 69 of them ran with the compare of GGML_HEXAGON_BATCHCACHE=2. No
compare found a difference, and the symbolic check found no violation.

The phone

The stage quick ran the 4B Q8_0 in the app configuration. It measured this
patch together with the patches before and after it and with a change of the
rows of the pointwise unary ops, which is not in the series:

- Against HEAD, tg32 at the depth 0 is +1.50 % and pp512 is +3.38 %. The next
  phone batch measures the three patches without the row change.
- For each decode token after a prompt of 64 tokens (LLAMA_HOSTPROF, medians
  of 21 tokens), the pack takes 199 us with the preset value and 2158 us with
  GGML_HEXAGON_BATCHCACHE_MULTI=0, and 21 of 21 tokens are replays. The time
  from the last response of a token to the first send of the next token is
  983 us and 1592 us.
- The logits hashes of a prompt of 1024 tokens and 16 decode tokens are the
  same with GGML_HEXAGON_BATCHCACHE_MULTI=0 and with the preset value. A second
  pass of the prompt into a cleared memory, which is a replay of the prompt
  graph, gives the hashes of the first pass.

